---@class mongodb_atlas.AiModelApiKeyResponse
---@field apiKeyId? string Identifier used to reference this API key in admin API calls.
---@field cloud? string Cloud provider scope for this API key. Use "ANY" for cloud-agnostic scope.
---@field createdAt? string UTC date when the API key was created. This parameter is formatted as an ISO 8601 timestamp.
---@field createdBy? string Name of the user that created this API key. If no user name is available, the user ID is returned.
---@field endpoint? string Server-computed endpoint hostname derived from `cloud` and `geography`. This field is read-only and must not be supplied in request bodies.
---@field geography? string Geography scope for this API key. Use "ANY" for geography-agnostic scope.
---@field groupId? string ID of the Atlas group this API key belongs to.
---@field lastUsedAt? string|distilled.Null UTC date when the API key was last used. This parameter is formatted as an ISO 8601 timestamp.
---@field maskedSecret? string A partially obfuscated version of the API key secret returned when the API key was created.
---@field name? string Arbitrary string identifier assigned to this API key for convenient identification.
---@field secret? distilled.Secret|distilled.Null The full API key secret used for interacting with the embedding / reranking service. Note: this will only be fully populated in the response to a create API key request. Responses to get, list, and update requests will not include the secret.
---@field status? string A string describing the current status of the API key.

