---@field compute? mongodb_atlas.ApiSearchComputeAutoScalingView

---Settings that control Search Node tier scaling based on load.
---@class mongodb_atlas.ApiSearchComputeAutoScalingView
---@field enabled? boolean Flag that indicates whether Atlas raises the Search Node tier when the nodes are under sustained load. If set to `true`, you must also set `maxInstanceTier`.
---@field maxInstanceTier? mongodb_atlas.ApiSearchComputeAutoScalingViewMaxInstanceTier|string Highest Search Node tier that Atlas can scale up to. Required when `enabled` is `true`.
---@field minInstanceTier? mongodb_atlas.ApiSearchComputeAutoScalingViewMinInstanceTier|string Lowest Search Node tier that Atlas can scale down to. Required when `scaleDownEnabled` is `true`. Scaling down is not supported yet, so setting this returns an error.
---@field scaleDownEnabled? boolean Flag that indicates whether Atlas lowers the Search Node tier when load drops. Takes effect only when `enabled` is `true`. If set to `true`, you must also set `minInstanceTier`. Scaling down is not supported yet, so setting this to `true` returns an error.

---Highest Search Node tier that Atlas can scale up to. Required when `enabled` is `true`.
