---Group of Network Peering connection settings.
---@class mongodb_atlas.AwsNetworkPeeringConnectionSettings
---@field accepterRegionName string Amazon Web Services (AWS) region where the Virtual Peering Connection (VPC) that you peered with the MongoDB Cloud VPC resides. The resource returns `null` if your VPC and the MongoDB Cloud VPC reside in the same region.
---@field awsAccountId string Unique twelve-digit string that identifies the Amazon Web Services (AWS) account that owns the VPC that you peered with the MongoDB Cloud VPC.
---@field connectionId? string Unique string that identifies the peering connection on AWS.
---@field containerId string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the MongoDB Cloud network container that contains the specified network peering connection.
---@field errorStateName? mongodb_atlas.AwsNetworkPeeringConnectionSettingsErrorStateName Type of error that can be returned when requesting an Amazon Web Services (AWS) peering connection. The resource returns `null` if the request succeeded.
---@field id? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the network peering connection.
---@field providerName? mongodb_atlas.AwsNetworkPeeringConnectionSettingsProviderName Cloud service provider that serves the requested network peering connection.
---@field routeTableCidrBlock string Internet Protocol (IP) addresses expressed in Classless Inter-Domain Routing (CIDR) notation of the VPC's subnet that you want to peer with the MongoDB Cloud VPC.
---@field statusName? mongodb_atlas.AwsNetworkPeeringConnectionSettingsStatusName State of the network peering connection at the time you made the request.
---@field vpcId string Unique string that identifies the VPC on Amazon Web Services (AWS) that you want to peer with the MongoDB Cloud VPC.

