---Specifications for on-demand policy.
---@class mongodb_atlas.BackupComplianceOnDemandPolicyItem
---@field frequencyInterval mongodb_atlas.BackupComplianceOnDemandPolicyItemFrequencyInterval Number that indicates the frequency interval for a set of snapshots. MongoDB Cloud ignores this setting for non-hourly policy items in Backup Compliance Policy settings.
---@field frequencyType mongodb_atlas.BackupComplianceOnDemandPolicyItemFrequencyType Human-readable label that identifies the frequency type associated with the backup policy.
---@field id? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies this backup policy item.
---@field retentionUnit mongodb_atlas.BackupComplianceOnDemandPolicyItemRetentionUnit Unit of time in which MongoDB Cloud measures snapshot retention.
---@field retentionValue number Duration in days, weeks, months, or years that MongoDB Cloud retains the snapshot. For less frequent policy items, MongoDB Cloud requires that you specify a value greater than or equal to the value specified for more frequent policy items. For example: If the hourly policy item specifies a retention of two days, you must specify two days or greater for the retention of the weekly policy item.

---Number that indicates the frequency interval for a set of snapshots. MongoDB Cloud ignores this setting for non-hourly policy items in Backup Compliance Policy settings.
