---Specifications for scheduled policy.
---@class mongodb_atlas.BackupComplianceScheduledPolicyItem
---@field frequencyInterval mongodb_atlas.BackupComplianceScheduledPolicyItemFrequencyInterval Number that indicates the frequency interval for a set of Snapshots. A value of `1` specifies the first instance of the corresponding `frequencyType`. - In a yearly policy item, `1` indicates that the yearly Snapshot occurs on the first day of January and `12` indicates the first day of December. - In a monthly policy item, `1` indicates that the monthly Snapshot occurs on the first day of the month and `40` indicates the last day of the month. - In a weekly policy item, `1` indicates that the weekly Snapshot occurs on Monday and `7` indicates Sunday. - In an hourly policy item, you can set the frequency interval to `1`, `2`, `4`, `6`, `8`, or `12`. For hourly policy items for NVMe clusters, MongoDB Cloud accepts only `12` as the frequency interval value. MongoDB Cloud ignores this setting for non-hourly policy items in Backup Compliance Policy settings.
---@field frequencyType mongodb_atlas.BackupComplianceScheduledPolicyItemFrequencyType Human-readable label that identifies the frequency type associated with the backup policy.
---@field id? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies this backup policy item.
---@field retentionUnit mongodb_atlas.BackupComplianceScheduledPolicyItemRetentionUnit Unit of time in which MongoDB Cloud measures Snapshot retention.
---@field retentionValue number Duration in days, weeks, months, or years that MongoDB Cloud retains the Snapshot. For less frequent policy items, MongoDB Cloud requires that you specify a value greater than or equal to the value specified for more frequent policy items. For example: If the hourly policy item specifies a retention of two days, you must specify two days or greater for the retention of the weekly policy item.

---Number that indicates the frequency interval for a set of Snapshots. A value of `1` specifies the first instance of the corresponding `frequencyType`.
