---@class mongodb_atlas.ClusterFlexProviderSettings
---@field autoScaling? mongodb_atlas.ClusterFlexProviderSettingsAutoScaling Range of instance sizes to which your cluster can scale.
---@field diskTypeName? mongodb_atlas.ClusterFlexProviderSettingsDiskTypeName Disk type that corresponds to the host's root volume for Azure instances. If omitted, the default disk type for the selected `providerSettings.instanceSizeName` applies.
---@field instanceSizeName? mongodb_atlas.ClusterFlexProviderSettingsInstanceSizeName Cluster tier, with a default storage and memory capacity, that applies to all the data-bearing hosts in your cluster.
---@field regionName? mongodb_atlas.ClusterFlexProviderSettingsRegionName Microsoft Azure Regions.
---@field backingProviderName? mongodb_atlas.ClusterFlexProviderSettingsBackingProviderName Cloud service provider on which MongoDB Cloud provisioned the multi-tenant host. The resource returns this parameter when `providerSettings.providerName` is `TENANT` and `providerSetting.instanceSizeName` is `M0`, `M2` or `M5`. Please note that using an `instanceSize` of M2 or M5 will create a Flex cluster instead. Support for the `instanceSize` of M2 or M5 will be discontinued in January 2026. We recommend using the Create Flex Cluster API for such configurations moving forward.
---@field effectiveInstanceSizeName? mongodb_atlas.ClusterFlexProviderSettingsEffectiveInstanceSizeName The true tenant instance size. This is present to support backwards compatibility for deprecated provider types and/or instance sizes.
---@field providerName string
---@field diskIOPS? number Maximum Disk Input/Output Operations per Second (IOPS) that the database host can perform.
---@field encryptEBSVolume? boolean Flag that indicates whether the Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS) encryption feature encrypts the host's root volume for both data at rest within the volume and for data moving between the volume and the cluster. Clusters always have this setting enabled.
---@field volumeType? mongodb_atlas.ClusterFlexProviderSettingsVolumeType Disk Input/Output Operations per Second (IOPS) setting for Amazon Web Services (AWS) storage that you configure only for AWS. Specify whether Disk Input/Output Operations per Second (IOPS) must not exceed the default Input/Output Operations per Second (IOPS) rate for the selected volume size (`STANDARD`), or must fall within the allowable Input/Output Operations per Second (IOPS) range for the selected volume size (`PROVISIONED` or `HIGH_PERFORMANCE`). NVMe clusters require either `PROVISIONED` or `HIGH_PERFORMANCE`.

---Range of instance sizes to which your cluster can scale.
---@class mongodb_atlas.ClusterFlexProviderSettingsAutoScaling
---@field compute? mongodb_atlas.ClusterFlexProviderSettingsAutoScalingCompute Collection of settings that configures how a cluster might scale its cluster tier and whether the cluster can scale down. Cluster tier auto-scaling is unavailable for clusters using Low CPU or NVME storage classes.

---Collection of settings that configures how a cluster might scale its cluster tier and whether the cluster can scale down. Cluster tier auto-scaling is unavailable for clusters using Low CPU or NVME storage classes.
