---@class mongodb_atlas.ClusterOutageSimulation
---@field clusterName? string Human-readable label that identifies the cluster that undergoes outage simulation.
---@field expirationDate? string Date and time when MongoDB Cloud expires the outage simulation. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC. If not provided, defaults to 3 days from the start date.
---@field groupId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal character string that identifies the project that contains the cluster to undergo outage simulation.
---@field id? string Unique 24-hexadecimal character string that identifies the outage simulation.
---@field outageFilters? mongodb_atlas.ClusterOutageSimulationOutageFiltersList List of settings that specify the type of cluster outage simulation.
---@field startRequestDate? string Date and time when MongoDB Cloud started the regional outage simulation. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.
---@field state? mongodb_atlas.ClusterOutageSimulationState Phase of the outage simulation. | State | Indication | |-------------|------------| | `START_REQUESTED` | User has requested cluster outage simulation.| | `STARTING` | MongoDB Cloud is starting cluster outage simulation.| | `SIMULATING` | MongoDB Cloud is simulating cluster outage.| | `RECOVERY_REQUESTED` | User has requested recovery from the simulated outage.| | `RECOVERING` | MongoDB Cloud is recovering the cluster from the simulated outage.| | `COMPLETE` | MongoDB Cloud has completed the cluster outage simulation.|

---List of settings that specify the type of cluster outage simulation.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.ClusterOutageSimulationOutageFiltersList mongodb_atlas.AtlasClusterOutageSimulationOutageFilter[]

---Phase of the outage simulation.
---
---| State       | Indication |
---|-------------|------------|
---| `START_REQUESTED`    | User has requested cluster outage simulation.|
---| `STARTING`           | MongoDB Cloud is starting cluster outage simulation.|
---| `SIMULATING`         | MongoDB Cloud is simulating cluster outage.|
---| `RECOVERY_REQUESTED` | User has requested recovery from the simulated outage.|
---| `RECOVERING`         | MongoDB Cloud is recovering the cluster from the simulated outage.|
---| `COMPLETE`           | MongoDB Cloud has completed the cluster outage simulation.|
---@alias mongodb_atlas.ClusterOutageSimulationState "START_REQUESTED"|"STARTING"|"SIMULATING"|"RECOVERY_REQUESTED"|"RECOVERING"|"COMPLETE"

