---@class mongodb_atlas.DataLakeAzureBlobStore
---@field region? mongodb_atlas.DataLakeAzureBlobStoreRegion Physical location where MongoDB Cloud deploys your AWS-hosted MongoDB cluster nodes. The region you choose can affect network latency for clients accessing your databases. When MongoDB Cloud deploys a dedicated cluster, it checks if a VPC or VPC connection exists for that provider and region. If not, MongoDB Cloud creates them as part of the deployment. MongoDB Cloud assigns the VPC a CIDR block. To limit a new VPC peering connection to one CIDR block and region, create the connection first. Deploy the cluster after the connection starts.
---@field clusterName? string Human-readable label of the MongoDB Cloud cluster on which the store is based.
---@field projectId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the project.
---@field readConcern? mongodb_atlas.DataLakeAtlasStoreReadConcern
---@field readPreference? mongodb_atlas.DataLakeAtlasStoreReadPreference
---@field allowInsecure? boolean Flag that validates the scheme in the specified URLs. If `true`, allows insecure `HTTP` scheme, doesn't verify the server's certificate chain and hostname, and accepts any certificate with any hostname presented by the server. If `false`, allows secure `HTTPS` scheme only.
---@field defaultFormat? string Default format that Data Lake assumes if it encounters a file without an extension while searching the `storeName`. If omitted, Data Lake attempts to detect the file type by processing a few bytes of the file. The specified format only applies to the URLs specified in the **databases.[n].collections.[n].dataSources** object.
---@field urls? mongodb_atlas.DataLakeAzureBlobStoreUrlsList Comma-separated list of publicly accessible HTTP URLs where data is stored. You can't specify URLs that require authentication.
---@field containerName? string Human-readable label that identifies the name of the container.
---@field delimiter? string Delimiter.
---@field prefix? string Prefix.
---@field public? boolean Flag that indicates whether the blob store is public. If set to `true`, MongoDB Cloud doesn't use the configured Azure service principal to access the blob store. If set to `false`, the configured Azure service principal must include permissions to access the blob store.
---@field replacementDelimiter? string Replacement Delimiter.
---@field serviceURL? string Service URL.
---@field bucket? string Human-readable label that identifies the Google Cloud Storage bucket.
---@field name? string Human-readable label that identifies the data store. The **databases.[n].collections.[n].dataSources.[n].storeName** field references this values as part of the mapping configuration. To use MongoDB Cloud as a data store, the data lake requires a serverless instance or an `M10` or higher cluster.
---@field provider string
---@field additionalStorageClasses? mongodb_atlas.DataLakeAzureBlobStoreAdditionalStorageClassesList Collection of AWS S3 [storage classes](https://aws.amazon.com/s3/storage-classes/). Atlas Data Lake includes the files in these storage classes in the query results.
---@field includeTags? boolean Flag that indicates whether to use S3 tags on the files in the given path as additional partition attributes. If set to `true`, data lake adds the S3 tags as additional partition attributes and adds new top-level BSON elements associating each tag to each document.

---AWS S3 [storage class](https://aws.amazon.com/s3/storage-classes/) where the files to include in the results are stored.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.DataLakeAzureBlobStoreAdditionalStorageClassesItem "STANDARD"|"INTELLIGENT_TIERING"|"STANDARD_IA"

---Collection of AWS S3 [storage classes](https://aws.amazon.com/s3/storage-classes/). Atlas Data Lake includes the files in these storage classes in the query results.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.DataLakeAzureBlobStoreAdditionalStorageClassesList mongodb_atlas.DataLakeAzureBlobStoreAdditionalStorageClassesItem[]

