---Disk backup snapshot Export Bucket Request.
---@class mongodb_atlas.DiskBackupSnapshotAzureExportBucketRequestInput
---@field cloudProvider mongodb_atlas.DiskBackupSnapshotAzureExportBucketRequestInputCloudProvider|string Human-readable label that identifies the cloud provider.
---@field bucketName? string The name of the Azure Storage Container to export to. This can be omitted and computed from the `serviceUrl` if the `serviceUrl` includes a Azure Storage Container name. For example a `serviceUrl` of `https://examplestorageaccount.blob.core.windows.net/exportcontainer` will yield a computed `bucketName` of `exportcontainer`. If the `serviceUrl` does not include a Container name, this field is required.
---@field roleId string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the Azure Cloud Provider Access Role that MongoDB Cloud uses to access the Azure Blob Storage Container.
---@field serviceUrl string URL of the Azure Storage Account to export to. For example: `https://examplestorageaccount.blob.core.windows.net/exportcontainer`. Only standard endpoints (with `blob.core.windows.net`) are supported.
---@field tenantId? string UUID that identifies the Azure Active Directory Tenant ID. Deprecated: this field is ignored; the `tenantId` of the Cloud Provider Access role (from `roleId`) is used.

---Human-readable label that identifies the cloud provider.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.DiskBackupSnapshotAzureExportBucketRequestInputCloudProvider "AZURE"

