---@class mongodb_atlas.DiskBackupSnapshotRestoreJob
---@field cancelled? boolean Flag that indicates whether someone canceled this restore job.
---@field components? mongodb_atlas.DiskBackupSnapshotRestoreJobComponentsList Information on the restore job for each replica set in the sharded cluster.
---@field deliveryType mongodb_atlas.DiskBackupSnapshotRestoreJobDeliveryType Human-readable label that categorizes the restore job to create.
---@field deliveryUrl? mongodb_atlas.DiskBackupSnapshotRestoreJobDeliveryUrlList One or more Uniform Resource Locators (URLs) that point to the compressed snapshot files for manual download. MongoDB Cloud returns this parameter when `"deliveryType" : "download"`.
---@field desiredTimestamp? mongodb_atlas.ApiBSONTimestampView
---@field expired? boolean Flag that indicates whether the restore job expired.
---@field expiresAt? string Date and time when the restore job expires. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.
---@field failed? boolean Flag that indicates whether the restore job failed.
---@field finishedAt? string Date and time when the restore job completed. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.
---@field id? string Unique 24-hexadecimal character string that identifies the restore job.
---@field links? mongodb_atlas.DiskBackupSnapshotRestoreJobLinksList List of one or more Uniform Resource Locators (URLs) that point to API sub-resources, related API resources, or both. RFC 5988 outlines these relationships.
---@field oplogInc? number Oplog operation number from which you want to restore this snapshot. This number represents the second part of an Oplog timestamp. The resource returns this parameter when `"deliveryType" : "pointInTime"` and `oplogTs` exceeds `0`.
---@field oplogTs? number Date and time from which you want to restore this snapshot. This parameter expresses this timestamp in the number of seconds that have elapsed since the UNIX epoch. This number represents the first part of an Oplog timestamp. The resource returns this parameter when `"deliveryType" : "pointInTime"` and `oplogTs` exceeds `0`.
---@field pointInTimeUTCSeconds? number Date and time from which MongoDB Cloud restored this snapshot. This parameter expresses this timestamp in the number of seconds that have elapsed since the UNIX epoch. The resource returns this parameter when `"deliveryType" : "pointInTime"` and `pointInTimeUTCSeconds` exceeds `0`.
---@field privateDownloadDeliveryUrls? mongodb_atlas.DiskBackupSnapshotRestoreJobPrivateDownloadDeliveryUrlsList One or more Uniform Resource Locators (URLs) that point to the compressed snapshot files for manual download and the corresponding private endpoint(s). MongoDB Cloud returns this parameter when `"deliveryType" : "download"` and the download can be performed privately.
---@field snapshotId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal character string that identifies the snapshot.
---@field targetClusterName? string Human-readable label that identifies the target cluster to which the restore job restores the snapshot. The resource returns this parameter when `"deliveryType":` `"automated"`. Required for `automated` and `pointInTime` restore types.
---@field targetGroupId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the target project for the specified `targetClusterName`. Required for `automated` and `pointInTime` restore types.
---@field timestamp? string Date and time when MongoDB Cloud took the snapshot associated with `snapshotId`. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.

