---@class mongodb_atlas.DownloadGroupClusterLogRequest
---@field groupId string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies your project. Use the [/groups](#tag/Projects/operation/listProjects) endpoint to retrieve all projects to which the authenticated user has access. **NOTE**: Groups and projects are synonymous terms. Your group id is the same as your project id. For existing groups, your group/project id remains the same. The resource and corresponding endpoints use the term groups.
---@field hostName string Human-readable label that identifies the host that stores the log files that you want to download.
---@field logName mongodb_atlas.DownloadGroupClusterLogRequestLogName|string Human-readable label that identifies the log file that you want to return. To return audit logs, enable *Database Auditing* for the specified project.
---@field envelope? boolean Flag that indicates whether Application wraps the response in an `envelope` JSON object. Some API clients cannot access the HTTP response headers or status code. To remediate this, set envelope=true in the query. Endpoints that return a list of results use the results object as an envelope. Application adds the status parameter to the response body.
---@field endDate? number Specifies the date and time for the ending point of the range of log messages to retrieve, in the number of seconds that have elapsed since the UNIX epoch. This value will default to 24 hours after the start date. If the start date is also unspecified, the value will default to the time of the request.
---@field startDate? number Specifies the date and time for the starting point of the range of log messages to retrieve, in the number of seconds that have elapsed since the UNIX epoch. This value will default to 24 hours prior to the end date. If the end date is also unspecified, the value will default to 24 hours prior to the time of the request.

---@alias mongodb_atlas.DownloadGroupClusterLogRequestLogName "mongodb"|"mongos"|"mongodb-audit-log"|"mongos-audit-log"

---@class mongodb_atlas.DownloadGroupClusterLogResponse

---@class mongodb_atlas.DownloadGroupClusterOnlineArchiveQueryLogsRequest
---@field groupId string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies your project. Use the [/groups](#tag/Projects/operation/listProjects) endpoint to retrieve all projects to which the authenticated user has access. **NOTE**: Groups and projects are synonymous terms. Your group id is the same as your project id. For existing groups, your group/project id remains the same. The resource and corresponding endpoints use the term groups.
---@field clusterName string Human-readable label that identifies the cluster that contains the collection for which you want to return the query logs from one online archive.
---@field envelope? boolean Flag that indicates whether Application wraps the response in an `envelope` JSON object. Some API clients cannot access the HTTP response headers or status code. To remediate this, set envelope=true in the query. Endpoints that return a list of results use the results object as an envelope. Application adds the status parameter to the response body.
---@field startDate? number Date and time that specifies the starting point for the range of log messages to return. This resource expresses this value in the number of seconds that have elapsed since the [UNIX epoch](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix_time).
---@field endDate? number Date and time that specifies the end point for the range of log messages to return. This resource expresses this value in the number of seconds that have elapsed since the [UNIX epoch](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix_time).
---@field archiveOnly? boolean Flag that indicates whether to download logs for queries against your online archive only or both your online archive and cluster.

---@class mongodb_atlas.DownloadGroupClusterOnlineArchiveQueryLogsResponse

---@class mongodb_atlas.DownloadGroupDataFederationQueryLogsRequest
---@field groupId string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies your project. Use the [/groups](#tag/Projects/operation/listProjects) endpoint to retrieve all projects to which the authenticated user has access. **NOTE**: Groups and projects are synonymous terms. Your group id is the same as your project id. For existing groups, your group/project id remains the same. The resource and corresponding endpoints use the term groups.
---@field tenantName string Human-readable label that identifies the federated database instance for which you want to download query logs.
