---Group of settings that configure a MongoDB Flex cluster.
---@class mongodb_atlas.FlexClusterDescription20241113
---@field backupSettings? mongodb_atlas.FlexBackupSettings20241113
---@field clusterType? mongodb_atlas.FlexClusterDescription20241113ClusterType Flex cluster topology.
---@field connectionStrings? mongodb_atlas.FlexConnectionStrings20241113
---@field createDate? string Date and time when MongoDB Cloud created this instance. This parameter expresses its value in ISO 8601 format in UTC.
---@field databaseEdition? mongodb_atlas.FlexClusterDescription20241113DatabaseEdition Available in Public Preview: Optional field that indicates whether your tenant cluster will be upgraded to Atlas INFINITE or CORE.
---@field groupId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal character string that identifies the project.
---@field id? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the instance.
---@field links? mongodb_atlas.FlexClusterDescription20241113LinksList List of one or more Uniform Resource Locators (URLs) that point to API sub-resources, related API resources, or both. RFC 5988 outlines these relationships.
---@field mongoDBVersion? string Version of MongoDB that the instance runs.
---@field name? string Human-readable label that identifies the instance.
---@field providerSettings mongodb_atlas.FlexProviderSettings20241113
---@field stateName? mongodb_atlas.FlexClusterDescription20241113StateName Human-readable label that indicates any current activity being taken on this cluster by the Atlas control plane. With the exception of CREATING and DELETING states, clusters should always be available and have a Primary node even when in states indicating ongoing activity. - `IDLE`: Atlas is making no changes to this cluster and all changes requested via the UI or API can be assumed to have been applied. - `CREATING`: A cluster being provisioned for the very first time returns state CREATING until it is ready for connections. Ensure IP Access List and DB Users are configured before attempting to connect. - `UPDATING`: A change requested via the UI, API, AutoScaling, or other scheduled activity is taking place. - `DELETING`: The cluster is in the process of deletion and will soon be deleted. - `REPAIRING`: One or more nodes in the cluster are being returned to service by the Atlas control plane. Other nodes should continue to provide service as normal.
---@field tags? mongodb_atlas.FlexClusterDescription20241113TagsList List that contains key-value pairs between 1 to 255 characters in length for tagging and categorizing the instance.
---@field terminationProtectionEnabled? boolean Flag that indicates whether termination protection is enabled on the cluster. If set to `true`, MongoDB Cloud won't delete the cluster. If set to `false`, MongoDB Cloud will delete the cluster.
---@field versionReleaseSystem? mongodb_atlas.FlexClusterDescription20241113VersionReleaseSystem Method by which the cluster maintains the MongoDB versions.

