---@field apiKey? distilled.Secret API key for authentication.
---@field region? mongodb_atlas.GcsLogIntegrationResponseOutputRegion Datadog site/region for log ingestion. Valid values: US1, US3, US5, EU, AP1, AP2, US1_FED.
---@field type mongodb_atlas.GcsLogIntegrationResponseOutputType Human-readable label that identifies the service to which you want to integrate with Atlas. The value must match the log integration type. This value cannot be modified after the integration is created.
---@field bucketName string Name of the bucket to store log files.
---@field prefixPath string Path prefix where the log files will be stored. Atlas will add further sub-directories based on the log type.
---@field roleId string Unique 24-character hexadecimal string that identifies the Atlas Cloud Provider Access role.
---@field otelEndpoint? string OpenTelemetry collector endpoint URL.
---@field otelSuppliedHeaders? mongodb_atlas.GcsLogIntegrationResponseOutputOtelSuppliedHeadersList HTTP headers for authentication and configuration. Maximum 10 headers, total size limit 2KB.
---@field hecToken? string HTTP Event Collector (HEC) token for authentication.
---@field hecUrl? string HTTP Event Collector (HEC) endpoint URL.
---@field storageAccountName? string Storage account name where logs will be stored.
---@field storageContainerName? string Storage container name for log files.
---@field id string Unique 24-character hexadecimal digit string that identifies the log integration configuration.
---@field logTypes mongodb_atlas.GcsLogIntegrationResponseOutputLogTypesList Array of log types exported by this integration.
---@field iamRoleId? string Unique 24-character hexadecimal string that identifies the AWS IAM role that Atlas uses to access the S3 bucket.
---@field kmsKey? string|distilled.Null AWS KMS key ID or ARN for server-side encryption (optional). If not provided, uses bucket default encryption settings.
---@field useLegacyPathStructure? boolean When true, uses the legacy daily-folder path structure compatible with Push-Based Log Export: `{prefix}/{cluster}/{hostname}/{logType}/{YYYY-MM-DD}/{timestamp}-{logType}.log`. When false (default), uses the flat timestamped structure: `{prefix}/{cluster}/{hostname}/{logType}/{timestamp}-{logType}.log`.

