---One or more settings that determine how the MongoDB Cloud creates this MongoDB index.
---@class mongodb_atlas.IndexOptions
---@field _2dsphereIndexVersion? number Index version number applied to the 2dsphere index. MongoDB 3.2 and later use version 3. Use this option to override the default version number. This option applies to the **2dsphere** index type only.
---@field background? boolean Flag that indicates whether MongoDB should build the index in the background. This applies to MongoDB databases running feature compatibility version 4.0 or earlier. MongoDB databases running FCV 4.2 or later build indexes using an optimized build process. This process holds the exclusive lock only at the beginning and end of the build process. The rest of the build process yields to interleaving read and write operations. MongoDB databases running FCV 4.2 or later ignore this option. This option applies to all index types.
---@field bits? number Number of precision applied to the stored geohash value of the location data. This option applies to the **2d** index type only.
---@field bucketSize? number Number of units within which to group the location values. You could group in the same bucket those location values within the specified number of units to each other. This option applies to the geoHaystack index type only. MongoDB 5.0 removed geoHaystack Indexes and the `geoSearch` command.
---@field columnstoreProjection? mongodb_atlas.IndexOptionsColumnstoreProjectionMap The `columnstoreProjection` document allows to include or exclude sub-schemas schema. One cannot combine inclusion and exclusion statements. Accordingly, the <value> can be either of the following: 1 or true to include the field and recursively all fields it is a prefix of in the index 0 or false to exclude the field and recursively all fields it is a prefix of from the index.
---@field default_language? string Human language that determines the list of stop words and the rules for the stemmer and tokenizer. This option accepts the supported languages using its name in lowercase English or the ISO 639-2 code. If you set this parameter to `"none"`, then the text search uses simple tokenization with no list of stop words and no stemming. This option applies to the **text** index type only.
---@field expireAfterSeconds? number Number of seconds that MongoDB retains documents in a Time To Live (TTL) index.
---@field hidden? boolean Flag that determines whether the index is hidden from the query planner. A hidden index is not evaluated as part of the query plan selection.
---@field language_override? string Human-readable label that identifies the document parameter that contains the override language for the document. This option applies to the **text** index type only.
---@field max? number Upper inclusive boundary to limit the longitude and latitude values. This option applies to the 2d index type only.
---@field min? number Lower inclusive boundary to limit the longitude and latitude values. This option applies to the 2d index type only.
---@field name? string Human-readable label that identifies this index. This option applies to all index types.
---@field partialFilterExpression? mongodb_atlas.IndexOptionsPartialFilterExpressionMap Rules that limit the documents that the index references to a filter expression. All MongoDB index types accept a `partialFilterExpression` option. `partialFilterExpression` can include following expressions: - equality (`"parameter" : "value"` or using the `$eq` operator) - `"$exists": true` , maximum: `$gt`, `$gte`, `$lt`, `$lte` comparisons - `$type` - `$and` (top-level only) This option applies to all index types.
---@field sparse? boolean Flag that indicates whether the index references documents that only have the specified parameter. These indexes use less space but behave differently in some situations like when sorting. The following index types default to sparse and ignore this option: `2dsphere`, `2d`, `geoHaystack`, `text`. Compound indexes that includes one or more indexes with `2dsphere` keys alongside other key types, only the `2dsphere` index parameters determine which documents the index references. If you run MongoDB 3.2 or later, use partial indexes. This option applies to all index types.
---@field storageEngine? mongodb_atlas.IndexOptionsStorageEngineMap Storage engine set for the specific index. This value can be set only at creation. This option uses the following format: `"storageEngine" : { "<storage-engine-name>" : "<options>" }` MongoDB validates storage engine configuration options when creating indexes. To support replica sets with members with different storage engines, MongoDB logs these options to the oplog during replication. This option applies to all index types.
---@field textIndexVersion? number Version applied to this text index. MongoDB 3.2 and later use version `3`. Use this option to override the default version number. This option applies to the **text** index type only.
---@field weights? mongodb_atlas.IndexOptionsWeightsMap Relative importance to place upon provided index parameters. This object expresses this as key/value pairs of index parameter and weight to apply to that parameter. You can specify weights for some or all the indexed parameters. The weight must be an integer between 1 and 99,999. MongoDB 5.0 and later can apply **weights** to **text** indexes only.

---The `columnstoreProjection` document allows to include or exclude sub-schemas schema. One cannot combine inclusion and exclusion statements. Accordingly, the <value> can be either of the following:
---1 or true to include the field and recursively all fields it is a prefix of in the index
---0 or false to exclude the field and recursively all fields it is a prefix of from the index.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.IndexOptionsColumnstoreProjectionMap { [string]: number }

---Rules that limit the documents that the index references to a filter expression. All MongoDB index types accept a `partialFilterExpression` option. `partialFilterExpression` can include following expressions:
---
---- equality (`"parameter" : "value"` or using the `$eq` operator)
---- `"$exists": true`
---, maximum: `$gt`, `$gte`, `$lt`, `$lte` comparisons
---- `$type`
---- `$and` (top-level only)
--- This option applies to all index types.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.IndexOptionsPartialFilterExpressionMap { [string]: any }

---Storage engine set for the specific index. This value can be set only at creation. This option uses the following format: `"storageEngine" : { "<storage-engine-name>" : "<options>" }` MongoDB validates storage engine configuration options when creating indexes. To support replica sets with members with different storage engines, MongoDB logs these options to the oplog during replication. This option applies to all index types.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.IndexOptionsStorageEngineMap { [string]: any }

---Relative importance to place upon provided index parameters. This object expresses this as key/value pairs of index parameter and weight to apply to that parameter. You can specify weights for some or all the indexed parameters. The weight must be an integer between 1 and 99,999. MongoDB 5.0 and later can apply **weights** to **text** indexes only.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.IndexOptionsWeightsMap { [string]: any }

---@class mongodb_atlas.InviteGroupServiceAccountRequest
---@field groupId string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies your project. Use the [/groups](#tag/Projects/operation/listProjects) endpoint to retrieve all projects to which the authenticated user has access. **NOTE**: Groups and projects are synonymous terms. Your group id is the same as your project id. For existing groups, your group/project id remains the same. The resource and corresponding endpoints use the term groups.
---@field clientId string The Client ID of the Service Account.
---@field envelope? boolean Flag that indicates whether Application wraps the response in an `envelope` JSON object. Some API clients cannot access the HTTP response headers or status code. To remediate this, set envelope=true in the query. Endpoints that return a list of results use the results object as an envelope. Application adds the status parameter to the response body.
---@field pretty? boolean Flag that indicates whether the response body should be in the prettyprint format.
---@field roles mongodb_atlas.InviteGroupServiceAccountRequestRolesList The Project permissions for the Service Account in the specified Project.

---The Project permissions for the Service Account in the specified Project.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.InviteGroupServiceAccountRequestRolesList string[]

---One service included in this invoice.
---@class mongodb_atlas.InvoiceLineItem
---@field cloudProvider? mongodb_atlas.InvoiceLineItemCloudProvider Code identifying the cloud provider this line item's usage is attributed to. Values map as follows: AWS is Amazon Web Services, GCP is Google Cloud, AZURE is Microsoft Azure, and ATLAS is other Atlas usage not tied to a specific cloud provider.
---@field clusterName? string Human-readable label that identifies the cluster that incurred the charge.
---@field created? string Date and time when MongoDB Cloud created this line item. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.
---@field discountCents? number Sum by which MongoDB discounted this line item. MongoDB Cloud expresses this value in cents (100ths of one US Dollar). The resource returns this parameter when a discount applies.
---@field endDate? string Date and time when when MongoDB Cloud finished charging for this line item. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.
---@field groupId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the project associated to this line item.
---@field groupName? string Human-readable label that identifies the project.
---@field note? string Comment that applies to this line item.
---@field percentDiscount? number Percentage by which MongoDB discounted this line item. The resource returns this parameter when a discount applies.
---@field quantity? number Number of units included for the line item. These can be expressions of storage (GB), time (hours), or other units.
---@field sku? string Human-readable description of the service that this line item provided. This Stock Keeping Unit (SKU) could be the instance type, a support charge, advanced security, or another service.
---@field startDate? string Date and time when MongoDB Cloud began charging for this line item. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.
---@field stitchAppName? string Human-readable label that identifies the Atlas App Services application associated with this line item.
---@field tags? mongodb_atlas.InvoiceLineItemTagsMap A map of key-value pairs corresponding to the tags associated with the line item resource.
---@field tierLowerBound? number Lower bound for usage amount range in current SKU tier. **NOTE**: `lineItems[n].tierLowerBound` appears only if your `lineItems[n].sku` is tiered.
---@field tierUpperBound? number Upper bound for usage amount range in current SKU tier. **NOTE**: `lineItems[n].tierUpperBound` appears only if your `lineItems[n].sku` is tiered.
---@field totalPriceCents? number Sum of the cost set for this line item. MongoDB Cloud expresses this value in cents (100ths of one US Dollar) and calculates this value as `unitPriceDollars` * `quantity` * 100.
---@field unit? string Element used to express what **quantity** this line item measures. This value can be elements of time, storage capacity, and the like.
---@field unitPriceDollars? number Value per **unit** for this line item expressed in US Dollars.

---Code identifying the cloud provider this line item's usage is attributed to. Values map as follows: AWS is Amazon Web Services, GCP is Google Cloud, AZURE is Microsoft Azure, and ATLAS is other Atlas usage not tied to a specific cloud provider.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.InvoiceLineItemCloudProvider "AWS"|"GCP"|"AZURE"|"ATLAS"

---A map of key-value pairs corresponding to the tags associated with the line item resource.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.InvoiceLineItemTagsMap { [string]: mongodb_atlas.InvoiceLineItemTagsValueList }

---A map of key-value pairs corresponding to the tags associated with the line item resource.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.InvoiceLineItemTagsValueList string[]

