---@class mongodb_atlas.LiveMigrationResponse
---@field _id? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the migration job.
---@field lagTimeSeconds? number|distilled.Null Replication lag between the source and destination clusters. Atlas returns this setting only during an active migration, before the cutover phase.
---@field migrationHosts? mongodb_atlas.LiveMigrationResponseMigrationHostsList List of hosts running MongoDB Agents. These Agents can transfer your MongoDB data between one source and one destination cluster.
---@field readyForCutover? boolean Flag that indicates the migrated cluster can be cut over to MongoDB Atlas.
---@field status? mongodb_atlas.LiveMigrationResponseStatus|distilled.Null Progress made in migrating one cluster to MongoDB Atlas. `NEW`: Someone scheduled a local cluster migration to MongoDB Atlas. `FAILED`: The cluster migration to MongoDB Atlas failed. `COMPLETE`: The cluster migration to MongoDB Atlas succeeded. `EXPIRED`: MongoDB Atlas prepares to begin the cut over of the migrating cluster when source and destination clusters have almost synchronized. If `"readyForCutover" : true`, this synchronization starts a timer of 120 hours. You can extend this timer. If the timer expires, MongoDB Atlas returns this status. `WORKING`: The cluster migration to MongoDB Atlas is performing one of the following tasks: - Preparing connections to source and destination clusters. - Replicating data from source to destination. - Verifying MongoDB Atlas connection settings. - Stopping replication after the cut over.

---List of hosts running MongoDB Agents. These Agents can transfer your MongoDB data between one source and one destination cluster.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.LiveMigrationResponseMigrationHostsList string[]

---Progress made in migrating one cluster to MongoDB Atlas.
---
---`NEW`: Someone scheduled a local cluster migration to MongoDB Atlas.
---
---`FAILED`: The cluster migration to MongoDB Atlas failed.
---
---`COMPLETE`: The cluster migration to MongoDB Atlas succeeded.
---
---`EXPIRED`: MongoDB Atlas prepares to begin the cut over of the migrating cluster when source and destination clusters have almost synchronized. If `"readyForCutover" : true`, this synchronization starts a timer of 120 hours. You can extend this timer. If the timer expires, MongoDB Atlas returns this status.
---
---`WORKING`: The cluster migration to MongoDB Atlas is performing one of the following tasks:
---
---- Preparing connections to source and destination clusters.
---- Replicating data from source to destination.
---- Verifying MongoDB Atlas connection settings.
---- Stopping replication after the cut over.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.LiveMigrationResponseStatus "NEW"|"WORKING"|"FAILED"|"COMPLETE"|"EXPIRED"

