---OAuth 2.0 client credentials configuration. Required when `authType` is `OAUTH2`. Secrets are never returned.
---@class mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigRequest
---@field clientAuthMethod mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigRequestClientAuthMethod|string How the client authenticates to the token endpoint. `CLIENT_SECRET` sends a shared secret. `PRIVATE_KEY_JWT` signs a client assertion with an Atlas-generated, Atlas-managed key. Register the returned JWKS URL with your identity provider.
---@field clientId string OAuth 2.0 client identifier registered with the token endpoint.
---@field clientSecret? string|distilled.Secret Shared client secret. Required when `clientAuthMethod` is `CLIENT_SECRET`, and rejected for `PRIVATE_KEY_JWT`. Encrypted at rest and never returned.
---@field scopes? mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigRequestScopesList Optional OAuth 2.0 scopes requested on the token, sent as a space delimited `scope` parameter. Applies to both client authentication methods.
---@field tokenEndpoint string OAuth 2.0 token endpoint URL. Must use HTTPS.
---@field tokenRequestParams? mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigRequestTokenRequestParamsMap Optional provider-specific parameters added to the token request, for example a resource indicator. Applies to both client authentication methods.

---How the client authenticates to the token endpoint. `CLIENT_SECRET` sends a shared secret. `PRIVATE_KEY_JWT` signs a client assertion with an Atlas-generated, Atlas-managed key. Register the returned JWKS URL with your identity provider.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigRequestClientAuthMethod "CLIENT_SECRET"|"PRIVATE_KEY_JWT"

---Optional OAuth 2.0 scopes requested on the token, sent as a space delimited `scope` parameter. Applies to both client authentication methods.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigRequestScopesList string[]

---Optional provider-specific parameters added to the token request, for example a resource indicator. Applies to both client authentication methods.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigRequestTokenRequestParamsMap { [string]: string }

---OAuth 2.0 configuration returned for a metric integration. Secrets are never returned.
---@class mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigResponse
---@field clientAuthMethod mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigResponseClientAuthMethod How the client authenticates to the token endpoint.
---@field clientId string OAuth 2.0 client identifier registered with the token endpoint.
---@field scopes? mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigResponseScopesList OAuth 2.0 scopes requested on the token.
---@field signingKeyInfo? mongodb_atlas.OAuthSigningKeyInfo
---@field tokenEndpoint string OAuth 2.0 token endpoint URL.
---@field tokenRequestParams? mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigResponseTokenRequestParamsMap Provider-specific parameters added to the token request.

---How the client authenticates to the token endpoint.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigResponseClientAuthMethod "CLIENT_SECRET"|"PRIVATE_KEY_JWT"

---OAuth 2.0 scopes requested on the token.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigResponseScopesList string[]

---Provider-specific parameters added to the token request.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.OAuthConfigResponseTokenRequestParamsMap { [string]: string }

---Read-only metadata for the Atlas-managed signing key used by `PRIVATE_KEY_JWT`. Present only for that method. Register the `jwksUri` with your identity provider. Atlas rotates the underlying key without changing this URL.
---@class mongodb_atlas.OAuthSigningKeyInfo
---@field algorithm? string Signing algorithm of the Atlas-managed key.
---@field createdAt? string When the currently active signing key was created. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.
---@field jwksUri? string Public JWKS URL serving this integration's signing keys. Fixed for the lifetime of the integration.
---@field kid? string Key ID stamped on client assertions, the `SHA-1` thumbprint of the key certificate in uppercase hexadecimal. Changes when Atlas rotates the key.

---@class mongodb_atlas.ObjectStoragePrivateEndpointResponse
---@field cloudProvider? mongodb_atlas.ObjectStoragePrivateEndpointResponseCloudProvider Human-readable label that identifies the cloud provider.
---@field errorMessage? string Error message for failures associated with the Object Storage private endpoint.
---@field id? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the Private Endpoint Service.
---@field privateEndpointConnectionName? string Connection name of the Private Endpoint.
---@field regionName? mongodb_atlas.ObjectStoragePrivateEndpointResponseRegionName Cloud provider region in which the Object Storage bucket is located. For cross-region endpoints, this differs from `vpcRegionName`, which is the region in which the VPC interface endpoint is deployed.
---@field status? mongodb_atlas.ObjectStoragePrivateEndpointResponseStatus State of the Object Storage private endpoint.
---@field vpcRegionName? mongodb_atlas.ObjectStoragePrivateEndpointResponseVpcRegionName Cloud provider region in which the VPC interface endpoint is deployed. Echoes `regionName` for same-region endpoints.

---Human-readable label that identifies the cloud provider.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.ObjectStoragePrivateEndpointResponseCloudProvider "AWS"

---Physical location where MongoDB Cloud deploys your AWS-hosted MongoDB cluster nodes. The region you choose can affect network latency for clients accessing your databases.
---When MongoDB Cloud deploys a dedicated cluster, it checks if a VPC or VPC connection exists for that provider and region. If not, MongoDB Cloud creates them as part of the deployment. MongoDB Cloud assigns the VPC a CIDR block.
---To limit a new VPC peering connection to one CIDR block and region, create the connection first. Deploy the cluster after the connection starts.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.ObjectStoragePrivateEndpointResponseRegionName "US_GOV_WEST_1"|"US_GOV_EAST_1"|"US_EAST_1"|"US_EAST_2"|"US_WEST_1"|"US_WEST_2"|"CA_CENTRAL_1"|"EU_NORTH_1"|"EU_WEST_1"|"EU_WEST_2"|"EU_WEST_3"|"EU_CENTRAL_1"|"AP_EAST_1"|"AP_NORTHEAST_1"|"AP_NORTHEAST_2"|"AP_NORTHEAST_3"|"AP_SOUTHEAST_1"|"AP_SOUTHEAST_2"|"AP_SOUTHEAST_3"|"AP_SOUTH_1"|"SA_EAST_1"|"CN_NORTH_1"|"CN_NORTHWEST_1"|"ME_SOUTH_1"|"AF_SOUTH_1"|"EU_SOUTH_1"|"GLOBAL"

---State of the Object Storage private endpoint.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.ObjectStoragePrivateEndpointResponseStatus "INITIATING"|"PENDING_ACCEPTANCE"|"ACTIVE"|"FAILED"|"PENDING_RECREATION"|"DELETING"

---Physical location where MongoDB Cloud deploys your AWS-hosted MongoDB cluster nodes. The region you choose can affect network latency for clients accessing your databases.
---When MongoDB Cloud deploys a dedicated cluster, it checks if a VPC or VPC connection exists for that provider and region. If not, MongoDB Cloud creates them as part of the deployment. MongoDB Cloud assigns the VPC a CIDR block.
---To limit a new VPC peering connection to one CIDR block and region, create the connection first. Deploy the cluster after the connection starts.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.ObjectStoragePrivateEndpointResponseVpcRegionName "US_GOV_WEST_1"|"US_GOV_EAST_1"|"US_EAST_1"|"US_EAST_2"|"US_WEST_1"|"US_WEST_2"|"CA_CENTRAL_1"|"EU_NORTH_1"|"EU_WEST_1"|"EU_WEST_2"|"EU_WEST_3"|"EU_CENTRAL_1"|"AP_EAST_1"|"AP_NORTHEAST_1"|"AP_NORTHEAST_2"|"AP_NORTHEAST_3"|"AP_SOUTHEAST_1"|"AP_SOUTHEAST_2"|"AP_SOUTHEAST_3"|"AP_SOUTH_1"|"SA_EAST_1"|"CN_NORTH_1"|"CN_NORTHWEST_1"|"ME_SOUTH_1"|"AF_SOUTH_1"|"EU_SOUTH_1"|"GLOBAL"

