---Additional meta information captured about this event. The response returns this parameter as a JSON object when the query parameter `includeRaw=true`. The list of fields in the raw document may change. Don't rely on raw values for formal monitoring.
---@class mongodb_atlas.Raw
---@field _t? string Unique identifier of event type.
---@field alertConfigId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the alert configuration related to the event.
---@field cid? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the project in which the event occurred.
---@field cre? string Date and time when this event occurred. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.
---@field description? string|distilled.Null Description of the event.
---@field gn? string Human-readable label that identifies the project.
---@field id? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the event.
---@field orgId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the organization to which these events apply.
---@field orgName? string Human-readable label that identifies the organization that contains the project.
---@field severity? mongodb_atlas.RawSeverity Severity of the event.

---@class mongodb_atlas.RawMetricAlertView
---@field acknowledgedUntil? string Date and time until which this alert has been acknowledged. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC. The resource returns this parameter if a MongoDB User previously acknowledged this alert. - To acknowledge this alert forever, set the parameter value to 100 years in the future. - To unacknowledge a previously acknowledged alert, do not set this parameter value.
---@field acknowledgementComment? string Comment that a MongoDB Cloud user submitted when acknowledging the alert.
---@field acknowledgingUsername? string MongoDB Cloud username of the person who acknowledged the alert. The response returns this parameter if a MongoDB Cloud user previously acknowledged this alert.
---@field alertConfigId string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the alert configuration that sets this alert.
---@field clusterName? string Human-readable label that identifies the cluster to which this alert applies. This resource returns this parameter for alerts of events impacting backups, replica sets, or sharded clusters.
---@field created string Date and time when MongoDB Cloud created this alert. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.
---@field currentValue? mongodb_atlas.RawMetricValueView
---@field eventTypeName mongodb_atlas.HostMetricEventTypeViewAlertable
---@field groupId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the project that owns this alert.
---@field hostnameAndPort? string Hostname and port of the host to which this alert applies. The resource returns this parameter for alerts of events impacting hosts or replica sets.
---@field id string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies this alert.
---@field lastNotified? string Date and time that any notifications were last sent for this alert. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC. The resource returns this parameter if MongoDB Cloud has sent notifications for this alert.
---@field links? mongodb_atlas.RawMetricAlertViewLinksList List of one or more Uniform Resource Locators (URLs) that point to API sub-resources, related API resources, or both. RFC 5988 outlines these relationships.
---@field metricName? string Name of the metric against which Atlas checks the configured `metricThreshold.threshold`. To learn more about the available metrics, see <a href="https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/alert-host-metrics/#std-label-measurement-types" target="_blank">Host Metrics</a>. **NOTE**: If you set `eventTypeName` to `OUTSIDE_SERVERLESS_METRIC_THRESHOLD`, you can specify only metrics available for serverless. To learn more, see <a href="https://dochub.mongodb.org/core/alert-config-serverless-measurements" target="_blank">Serverless Measurements</a>.
---@field orgId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal character string that identifies the organization that owns the project to which this alert applies.
---@field replicaSetName? string Name of the replica set to which this alert applies. The response returns this parameter for alerts of events impacting backups, hosts, or replica sets.
---@field resolved? string Date and time that this alert changed to `"status" : "CLOSED"`. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC. The resource returns this parameter once `"status" : "CLOSED"`.
---@field severity? mongodb_atlas.RawMetricAlertViewSeverity Severity of the event.
---@field status mongodb_atlas.RawMetricAlertViewStatus State of this alert at the time you requested its details. TRACKING indicates the alert condition exists but has not persisted for the minimum notification delay. OPEN indicates the alert condition currently exists. CLOSED indicates the alert condition has been resolved.
---@field updated string Date and time when someone last updated this alert. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.

---List of one or more Uniform Resource Locators (URLs) that point to API sub-resources, related API resources, or both. RFC 5988 outlines these relationships.
