---Replica Set alert notifies about different activities on replica set of mongod instances.
---@class mongodb_atlas.ReplicaSetAlertViewForNdsGroup
---@field acknowledgedUntil? string Date and time until which this alert has been acknowledged. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC. The resource returns this parameter if a MongoDB User previously acknowledged this alert. - To acknowledge this alert forever, set the parameter value to 100 years in the future. - To unacknowledge a previously acknowledged alert, do not set this parameter value.
---@field acknowledgementComment? string Comment that a MongoDB Cloud user submitted when acknowledging the alert.
---@field acknowledgingUsername? string MongoDB Cloud username of the person who acknowledged the alert. The response returns this parameter if a MongoDB Cloud user previously acknowledged this alert.
---@field alertConfigId string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the alert configuration that sets this alert.
---@field clusterName? string Human-readable label that identifies the cluster to which this alert applies. This resource returns this parameter for alerts of events impacting backups, replica sets, or sharded clusters.
---@field created string Date and time when MongoDB Cloud created this alert. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.
---@field eventTypeName mongodb_atlas.ReplicaSetEventTypeViewForNdsGroupAlertable
---@field groupId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies the project that owns this alert.
---@field hostnameAndPort? string Hostname and port of the host to which this alert applies. The resource returns this parameter for alerts of events impacting hosts or replica sets.
---@field id string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies this alert.
---@field lastNotified? string Date and time that any notifications were last sent for this alert. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC. The resource returns this parameter if MongoDB Cloud has sent notifications for this alert.
---@field links? mongodb_atlas.ReplicaSetAlertViewForNdsGroupLinksList List of one or more Uniform Resource Locators (URLs) that point to API sub-resources, related API resources, or both. RFC 5988 outlines these relationships.
---@field nonRunningHostIds? mongodb_atlas.ReplicaSetAlertViewForNdsGroupNonRunningHostIdsList List of unique 24-hexadecimal character strings that identify the replica set members that are not in PRIMARY nor SECONDARY state.
---@field orgId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal character string that identifies the organization that owns the project to which this alert applies.
---@field parentClusterId? string Unique 24-hexadecimal character string that identifies the parent cluster to which this alert applies. The parent cluster contains the sharded nodes. MongoDB Cloud returns this parameter only for alerts of events impacting sharded clusters.
---@field replicaSetName? string Name of the replica set to which this alert applies. The response returns this parameter for alerts of events impacting backups, hosts, or replica sets.
---@field resolved? string Date and time that this alert changed to `"status" : "CLOSED"`. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC. The resource returns this parameter once `"status" : "CLOSED"`.
---@field severity? mongodb_atlas.ReplicaSetAlertViewForNdsGroupSeverity Severity of the event.
---@field status mongodb_atlas.ReplicaSetAlertViewForNdsGroupStatus State of this alert at the time you requested its details. TRACKING indicates the alert condition exists but has not persisted for the minimum notification delay. OPEN indicates the alert condition currently exists. CLOSED indicates the alert condition has been resolved.
---@field updated string Date and time when someone last updated this alert. This parameter expresses its value in the ISO 8601 timestamp format in UTC.

