---@alias mongodb_atlas.ShardMetricsResponseWarningsItem "HOTSPOT"

---Conditions that MongoDB Cloud observed on this shard relative to the rest of the cluster. `HOTSPOT` means this shard's average CPU utilization is more than twice the average across all shards of the cluster. This is a cluster-scoped comparison, so its value depends on how loaded the other shards are and not only on this shard.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.ShardMetricsResponseWarningsList mongodb_atlas.ShardMetricsResponseWarningsItem[]

---Operations per second that the shard served over the last hour.
---@class mongodb_atlas.ShardOperations
---@field average number Average operations per second across the shard's nodes over the last hour.
---@field maximum number Highest operations per second that any one of the shard's nodes reached over the last hour.

---Balancing window configured on the sharded cluster. When configured, the balancer moves data only during the daily interval between `startTime` and `endTime`.
---@class mongodb_atlas.ShardingInsightsBalancingWindow
---@field endTime? string|distilled.Null Time of day at which the balancing window ends, in 24-hour `HH:MM` format as configured on the cluster. Present only when `status` is `CONFIGURED`.
---@field startTime? string|distilled.Null Time of day at which the balancing window starts, in 24-hour `HH:MM` format as configured on the cluster. Present only when `status` is `CONFIGURED`.
---@field status mongodb_atlas.ShardingInsightsBalancingWindowStatus State of the balancing window. `CONFIGURED` means the cluster restricts balancing to the interval between `startTime` and `endTime`. `NOT_CONFIGURED` means the balancer may run at any time. `FAILED_INITIAL_METRIC_PENDING` means MongoDB Cloud has not yet collected balancer metrics for a recently created or converted cluster. `FAILED_TO_DETERMINE` means the window could not be resolved.

---State of the balancing window. `CONFIGURED` means the cluster restricts balancing to the interval between `startTime` and `endTime`. `NOT_CONFIGURED` means the balancer may run at any time. `FAILED_INITIAL_METRIC_PENDING` means MongoDB Cloud has not yet collected balancer metrics for a recently created or converted cluster. `FAILED_TO_DETERMINE` means the window could not be resolved.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.ShardingInsightsBalancingWindowStatus "CONFIGURED"|"NOT_CONFIGURED"|"FAILED_TO_DETERMINE"|"FAILED_INITIAL_METRIC_PENDING"

---Cluster-level sharding state of one sharded cluster: shard count, balancer state, config server availability, and the configured balancing window.
---@class mongodb_atlas.ShardingInsightsResponse
---@field balancerState mongodb_atlas.ShardingInsightsResponseBalancerState State of the cluster balancer. `BALANCING` means a balancer round is in progress. `IDLE` means the balancer is enabled and no round is in progress. `DISABLED` means the balancer is turned off. `FAILED_TO_DETERMINE` means the balancer state could not be resolved.
---@field balancingWindow mongodb_atlas.ShardingInsightsBalancingWindow
---@field configServerStatus mongodb_atlas.ShardingInsightsResponseConfigServerStatus Availability of the cluster's config servers. `AVAILABLE` means at least one config server reported recently. `UNAVAILABLE` means config servers exist but none has reported recently. `FAILED_TO_DETERMINE` means availability could not be resolved.
---@field totalShards number Number of shards in the cluster.

---State of the cluster balancer. `BALANCING` means a balancer round is in progress. `IDLE` means the balancer is enabled and no round is in progress. `DISABLED` means the balancer is turned off. `FAILED_TO_DETERMINE` means the balancer state could not be resolved.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.ShardingInsightsResponseBalancerState "BALANCING"|"IDLE"|"DISABLED"|"FAILED_TO_DETERMINE"

---Availability of the cluster's config servers. `AVAILABLE` means at least one config server reported recently. `UNAVAILABLE` means config servers exist but none has reported recently. `FAILED_TO_DETERMINE` means availability could not be resolved.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.ShardingInsightsResponseConfigServerStatus "AVAILABLE"|"UNAVAILABLE"|"FAILED_TO_DETERMINE"

