---An atlas stream processor.
---@class mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessor
---@field _id? string Unique 24-hexadecimal character string that identifies the stream processor.
---@field effectiveTier mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorEffectiveTier Tier the stream processor is currently running on. The server sets this value from `tier` on create and on every start or restart, may move it within [`minTier`, `maxTier`] while autoscaling is enabled, and restores it to `tier` when autoscaling is disabled. Patching `tier` does not change it directly; the new tier takes effect at the next start or restart.
---@field failoverEnabled? boolean Flag that enables or disables failover for the stream processor.
---@field links? mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorLinksList List of one or more Uniform Resource Locators (URLs) that point to API sub-resources, related API resources, or both. RFC 5988 outlines these relationships.
---@field name? string Human-readable name of the stream processor.
---@field options? mongodb_atlas.StreamsOptions
---@field pipeline? mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorPipelineList Stream aggregation pipeline you want to apply to your streaming data.
---@field tier? mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorTier Baseline tier of the stream processor. The processor starts or restarts on this tier; `effectiveTier` reports the tier it is currently running.

---Tier the stream processor is currently running on. The server sets this value from `tier` on create and on every start or restart, may move it within [`minTier`, `maxTier`] while autoscaling is enabled, and restores it to `tier` when autoscaling is disabled. Patching `tier` does not change it directly; the new tier takes effect at the next start or restart.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorEffectiveTier "SP50"|"SP30"|"SP10"|"SP5"|"SP2"

