---Stream aggregation pipeline you want to apply to your streaming data.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorPipelineList mongodb_atlas.Document[]

---Desired status change to apply to a tenant's stream processors.
---@class mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorStatusInput
---@field mode? mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorStatusInputMode|string|distilled.Null Strategy for the processor: GRACEFUL - attempt to stop the processor, error if processor cannot be stopped. if stop was successful, start the processor in the new region with the latest checkpoint. FORCED - attempt to stop the processor, proceed to starting the processor in the new region with checkpoints disabled regardless of whether or not the stop succeeds.
---@field region? string|distilled.Null Name of the region against which to apply the status change. Required when `status` is `FAILED_OVER`; optional otherwise.
---@field status mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorStatusInputStatus|string Represents the desired action to apply to stream processors within a workspace, such as starting all processors, stopping all processors, or performing a bulk regional failover.

---Strategy for the processor: GRACEFUL - attempt to stop the processor, error if processor cannot be stopped. if stop was successful, start the processor in the new region with the latest checkpoint.  FORCED - attempt to stop the processor, proceed to starting the processor in the new region with checkpoints disabled regardless of whether or not the stop succeeds.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorStatusInputMode "GRACEFUL"|"FORCED"

---Represents the desired action to apply to stream processors within a workspace, such as starting all processors, stopping all processors, or performing a bulk regional failover.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorStatusInputStatus "STARTED"|"STOPPED"|"FAILED_OVER"

---Baseline tier of the stream processor. The processor starts or restarts on this tier; `effectiveTier` reports the tier it is currently running.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorTier "SP50"|"SP30"|"SP10"|"SP5"|"SP2"

---An atlas stream processor with optional stats.
---@class mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorWithStats
---@field _id string Unique 24-hexadecimal character string that identifies the stream processor.
---@field effectiveTier mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorWithStatsEffectiveTier Tier the stream processor is currently running on. The server sets this value from `tier` on create and on every start or restart, may move it within [`minTier`, `maxTier`] while autoscaling is enabled, and restores it to `tier` when autoscaling is disabled. Patching `tier` does not change it directly; the new tier takes effect at the next start or restart.
---@field eligibleForFailover? boolean Flag that indicates whether the stream processor is eligible for failover.
---@field failoverEnabled? boolean Flag that enables or disables failover for the stream processor.
---@field links? mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorWithStatsLinksList List of one or more Uniform Resource Locators (URLs) that point to API sub-resources, related API resources, or both. RFC 5988 outlines these relationships.
---@field name string Human-readable name of the stream processor.
---@field options? mongodb_atlas.StreamsOptions
---@field pipeline mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorWithStatsPipelineList Stream aggregation pipeline you want to apply to your streaming data.
---@field state string The state of the stream processor. Commonly occurring states are 'CREATED', 'STARTED', 'STOPPED' and 'FAILED'.
---@field stats? mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorWithStatsStatsMap The stats associated with the stream processor.
---@field tier? mongodb_atlas.StreamsProcessorWithStatsTier Baseline tier of the stream processor. The processor starts or restarts on this tier; `effectiveTier` reports the tier it is currently running.

