---Text Search Index Create Request.
---@class mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexCreateRequest
---@field collectionName string Label that identifies the collection to create an Atlas Search index in.
---@field database string Label that identifies the database that contains the collection to create an Atlas Search index in.
---@field name string Label that identifies this index. Within each namespace, names of all indexes in the namespace must be unique.
---@field type mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexCreateRequestType|string Type of the index. The default type is search.
---@field definition mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinition

---Type of the index. The default type is search.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexCreateRequestType "search"

---The text search index definition set by the user.
---@class mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinition
---@field analyzer? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinitionAnalyzer|string Specific pre-defined method chosen to convert database field text into searchable words. This conversion reduces the text of fields into the smallest units of text. These units are called a **term** or **token**. This process, known as tokenization, involves making the following changes to the text in fields: - extracting words - removing punctuation - removing accents - changing to lowercase - removing common words - reducing words to their root form (stemming) - changing words to their base form (lemmatization) MongoDB Cloud uses the process you select to build the Atlas Search index.
---@field analyzers? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinitionAnalyzersList List of user-defined methods to convert database field text into searchable words.
---@field mappings mongodb_atlas.SearchMappings
---@field numPartitions? number Number of index partitions. Allowed values are [1, 2, 4].
---@field searchAnalyzer? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinitionSearchAnalyzer|string Method applied to identify words when searching this index.
---@field sort? any Sort definition for the index. When defined, the index will be pre-sorted on the specified fields, which improves query sort performance for those fields. Supports two formats: simple format with field name and direction, or complex format with additional options. The `order` field is required (1=ascending, -1=descending).The `noData` field is optional and controls how missing values are sorted(default: "lowest").
---@field storedSource? any Flag that indicates whether to store all fields (true) on Atlas Search. By default, Atlas doesn't store (false) the fields on Atlas Search. Alternatively, you can specify an object that only contains the list of fields to store (include) or not store (exclude) on Atlas Search. Note that storing all fields (true) is not allowed for vector search indexes. To learn more, see Stored Source Fields.
---@field synonyms? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinitionSynonymsList Rule sets that map words to their synonyms in this index.
---@field typeSets? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinitionTypeSetsList Type sets for the index.

---Specific pre-defined method chosen to convert database field text into searchable words. This conversion reduces the text of fields into the smallest units of text. These units are called a **term** or **token**. This process, known as tokenization, involves making the following changes to the text in fields:
---
---- extracting words
---- removing punctuation
---- removing accents
---- changing to lowercase
---- removing common words
---- reducing words to their root form (stemming)
---- changing words to their base form (lemmatization)
--- MongoDB Cloud uses the process you select to build the Atlas Search index.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinitionAnalyzer "lucene.standard"|"lucene.simple"|"lucene.whitespace"|"lucene.keyword"|"lucene.arabic"|"lucene.armenian"|"lucene.basque"|"lucene.bengali"|"lucene.brazilian"|"lucene.bulgarian"|"lucene.catalan"|"lucene.chinese"|"lucene.cjk"|"lucene.czech"|"lucene.danish"|"lucene.dutch"|"lucene.english"|"lucene.finnish"|"lucene.french"|"lucene.galician"|"lucene.german"|"lucene.greek"|"lucene.hindi"|"lucene.hungarian"|"lucene.indonesian"|"lucene.irish"|"lucene.italian"|"lucene.japanese"|"lucene.korean"|"lucene.kuromoji"|"lucene.latvian"|"lucene.lithuanian"|"lucene.morfologik"|"lucene.nori"|"lucene.norwegian"|"lucene.persian"|"lucene.portuguese"|"lucene.romanian"|"lucene.russian"|"lucene.smartcn"|"lucene.sorani"|"lucene.spanish"|"lucene.swedish"|"lucene.thai"|"lucene.turkish"|"lucene.ukrainian"

---List of user-defined methods to convert database field text into searchable words.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinitionAnalyzersList mongodb_atlas.AtlasSearchAnalyzer[]

---Method applied to identify words when searching this index.
---@alias mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinitionSearchAnalyzer "lucene.standard"|"lucene.simple"|"lucene.whitespace"|"lucene.keyword"|"lucene.arabic"|"lucene.armenian"|"lucene.basque"|"lucene.bengali"|"lucene.brazilian"|"lucene.bulgarian"|"lucene.catalan"|"lucene.chinese"|"lucene.cjk"|"lucene.czech"|"lucene.danish"|"lucene.dutch"|"lucene.english"|"lucene.finnish"|"lucene.french"|"lucene.galician"|"lucene.german"|"lucene.greek"|"lucene.hindi"|"lucene.hungarian"|"lucene.indonesian"|"lucene.irish"|"lucene.italian"|"lucene.japanese"|"lucene.korean"|"lucene.kuromoji"|"lucene.latvian"|"lucene.lithuanian"|"lucene.morfologik"|"lucene.nori"|"lucene.norwegian"|"lucene.persian"|"lucene.portuguese"|"lucene.romanian"|"lucene.russian"|"lucene.smartcn"|"lucene.sorani"|"lucene.spanish"|"lucene.swedish"|"lucene.thai"|"lucene.turkish"|"lucene.ukrainian"

