---@class mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexResponse
---@field collectionName? string Label that identifies the collection that contains one or more Atlas Search indexes.
---@field database? string Label that identifies the database that contains the collection with one or more Atlas Search indexes.
---@field indexID? string Unique 24-hexadecimal digit string that identifies this Atlas Search index.
---@field latestDefinition? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinition
---@field latestDefinitionVersion? mongodb_atlas.SearchIndexDefinitionVersion
---@field name? string Label that identifies this index. Within each namespace, the names of all indexes must be unique.
---@field queryable? boolean Flag that indicates whether the index is queryable on the nodes currently receiving query traffic.
---@field status? mongodb_atlas.SearchIndexResponseStatus Condition of the search index when you made this request. - `DELETING`: The index is being deleted. - `FAILED` The index build failed. Indexes can enter the FAILED state due to an invalid index definition. - `STALE`: The index is queryable but has stopped replicating data from the indexed collection. Searches on the index may return out-of-date data. - `PENDING`: Atlas has not yet started building the index. - `BUILDING`: Atlas is building or re-building the index after an edit. - `READY`: The index is ready and can support queries.
---@field statusDetail? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexResponseStatusDetailList List of documents detailing index status on each host.
---@field type mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexResponseType Type of the index. The default type is search.
---@field synonymMappingStatus? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexResponseSynonymMappingStatus Status that describes this index's synonym mappings. This status appears only if the index has synonyms defined.
---@field synonymMappingStatusDetail? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexResponseSynonymMappingStatusDetailList A list of documents describing the status of the index's synonym mappings on each search host. Only appears if the index has synonyms defined.

---@class mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexResponseStatusDetailItem
---@field hostname? string Hostname that corresponds to the status detail.
---@field mainIndex? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexResponseStatusDetailItemMainIndex Contains status information about the active index.
---@field queryable? boolean Flag that indicates whether the index is queryable on the host.
---@field stagedIndex? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexResponseStatusDetailItemStagedIndex Contains status information about an index building in the background.
---@field status? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexResponseStatusDetailItemStatus Condition of the search index when you made this request. - `DELETING`: The index is being deleted. - `FAILED` The index build failed. Indexes can enter the FAILED state due to an invalid index definition. - `STALE`: The index is queryable but has stopped replicating data from the indexed collection. Searches on the index may return out-of-date data. - `PENDING`: Atlas has not yet started building the index. - `BUILDING`: Atlas is building or re-building the index after an edit. - `READY`: The index is ready and can support queries.

---Contains status information about the active index.
---@class mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexResponseStatusDetailItemMainIndex
---@field definition? mongodb_atlas.TextSearchIndexDefinition
---@field definitionVersion? mongodb_atlas.SearchIndexDefinitionVersion
---@field message? string Optional message describing an error.
---@field queryable? boolean Flag that indicates whether the index generation is queryable on the host.
