---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_group_cluster_shard_key_analysis_operations(input) end

---Return Measurements for All Shards of One Cluster
---
---Returns time series of the requested measurements for every shard of the specified sharded cluster, one series per shard and measurement. Each shard's series averages the readings of its member processes selected by `nodeType`. Each series carries one data point per `granularity` interval, starting at `start` and not passing `end`. A data point's `value` is `null` when MongoDB Cloud has no reading for that interval; this includes the first minutes after a cluster or shard is created, before its metrics are collected, so `null` must not be read as zero load. Set `period`, or set both `start` and `end`; when neither is set, the response covers the last hour. A request whose window and `granularity` would produce more than 1000 data points per series is rejected.
---
---`GET /api/atlas/v2/groups/{groupId}/clusters/{clusterName}/shardMetrics:listMeasurements`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input mongodb_atlas.ListGroupClusterShardMetricMeasurementsRequest
---@return mongodb_atlas.ClusterShardMeasurementsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_group_cluster_shard_metric_measurements(input) end

---Return All Shards in One Cluster
---
---Returns the size and load of every shard in one sharded cluster. Each shard reports the data it stores, the CPU utilization of its nodes, the read and write operations it served, and any conditions that MongoDB Cloud observed relative to the rest of the cluster. To retrieve more details about a shard such as the latency, cache throughput and open alerts, request with an exact replica set name.
---
---`GET /api/atlas/v2/groups/{groupId}/clusters/{clusterName}/shardMetrics`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input mongodb_atlas.ListGroupClusterShardMetricsRequest
---@return mongodb_atlas.PaginatedShardMetricsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_group_cluster_shard_metrics(input) end

---Return All Clusters in One Project
---
---Returns the details for all clusters in the specific project to which you have access. Clusters contain a group of hosts that maintain the same data set. The response includes clusters with asymmetrically-sized shards. This feature is not  available for serverless clusters.
---
---This endpoint can also be used on Flex clusters that were created using the [Create Cluster](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/api-resources-spec/v2/#tag/Clusters/operation/createCluster) endpoint or former M2/M5 clusters that have been migrated to Flex clusters until January 2026. Please use the List Flex Clusters endpoint for Flex clusters instead. Deprecated versions: v2-{2023-02-01}, v2-{2023-01-01}
---
---`GET /api/atlas/v2/groups/{groupId}/clusters`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input mongodb_atlas.ListGroupClustersRequest
---@return mongodb_atlas.PaginatedClusterDescription20240805? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_group_clusters(input) end

